<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>{title} | PointCast</title><meta name="description" content={description}></head><body><header><a href="/">POINTCAST ↗</a><span>THE DATA FIELD GUIDE / 2026</span></header><main><section class="hero"><span class="badge">FIELD NOTE 02 · HOME</span><h1>What rent<br>looked like.</h1><p class="intro">Four South Bay cities, one survey window, and a reminder that an estimate comes with a margin of error.</p></section><figure class="art" style="margin:0"><img src="/data-stories/rent-illustration.png" alt="" width="1536" height="1024" style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:2px solid #192638;border-radius:20px"><figcaption>Conceptual illustration · not a map or data graphic</figcaption></figure><section class="panel dark"><span class="tag">THE MEASURE</span><h2>Rent, with the utilities folded in.</h2><p>Median monthly gross rent is the midpoint of qualifying renter households' contract rent plus estimated tenant-paid utilities and fuels. These are pooled 2020–2024 ACS five-year estimates for incorporated city limits, in dollars per month.</p><p>They describe households in the survey period—not current asking rents, a 2024-only count, or an individual household’s affordability.</p></section><section class="panel"><span class="tag">CENSUS B25064 / 2020–2024</span><h2>Four places, four estimates.</h2><p>The bar starts at $0 and ends at the estimate. The coral band marks the reported 90% margin of error around it. Sampling uncertainty is only one source of error.</p><div class="axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>$0</span><span>$2,000</span><span>$4,000 / month</span></div><div class="rentrow"><strong>Hermosa Beach</strong><div class="track" aria-hidden="true"><div class="bar" style="width:72.175%"></div><div class="range" style="left:67.275%;width:9.8%"></div></div><strong>$2,887 ± $196</strong></div><div class="rentrow"><strong>Manhattan Beach</strong><div class="track" aria-hidden="true"><div class="bar" style="width:86.225%"></div><div class="range" style="left:79.975%;width:12.5%"></div></div><strong>$3,449 ± $250</strong></div><div class="rentrow"><strong>Redondo Beach</strong><div class="track" aria-hidden="true"><div class="bar" style="width:67.275%"></div><div class="range" style="left:65.5%;width:3.55%"></div></div><strong>$2,691 ± $71</strong></div><div class="rentrow"><strong>Torrance</strong><div class="track" aria-hidden="true"><div class="bar" style="width:57.0%"></div><div class="range" style="left:55.7%;width:2.6%"></div></div><strong>$2,280 ± $52</strong></div><p>Margins overlap in some comparisons; the graphic alone does not establish whether differences are statistically significant.</p><details><summary>View source values and geography IDs</summary><table><thead><tr><th>City</th><th>ACS GEO_ID</th><th>Median gross rent</th><th>90% margin of error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hermosa Beach</td><td>1600000US0633364</td><td>$2,887</td><td>± $196</td></tr><tr><td>Manhattan Beach</td><td>1600000US0645400</td><td>$3,449</td><td>± $250</td></tr><tr><td>Redondo Beach</td><td>1600000US0660018</td><td>$2,691</td><td>± $71</td></tr><tr><td>Torrance</td><td>1600000US0680000</td><td>$2,280</td><td>± $52</td></tr></tbody></table></details></section><section class="panel"><h2>Read the fine print.</h2><p>Source: U.S. Census Bureau, 2024 ACS 5-year table B25064. <a href="https://www.census.gov/data/developers/about/terms-of-service.html">Census data reuse information ↗</a> ACS estimates are subject to sampling and nonsampling error. The margin is not a range of individual rents or a measure of all uncertainty.</p><p><a href="https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/summary_file/2024/table-based-SF/data/5YRData/acsdt5y2024-b25064.dat">Official table file ↗</a> · <a href="https://api.census.gov/data/2024/acs/acs5/groups/B25064.html">Variable definitions ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/guidance/statistical-testing-tool.html">Statistical testing guidance ↗</a></p><p>Downloaded November 3, 2026. Source SHA-256: <code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">b36e6dc1fcef36b8b307d31b37517b64c80d8b9c70d48c9b1894242860f42eb0</code>.</p></section><p><a href="/data-stories/earthquakes/">Previous field note: The ground →</a></p></main><footer><a href="/">POINTCAST</a> · A field guide to the data around us.</footer></body></html><style is:global> *{box-sizing:border-box}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.art{margin:0}.art img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:2px solid #192638;border-radius:20px}.art figcaption{font-size:.75rem;margin-top:8px}body{margin:0;background:#f3ecd9;color:#192638;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif}a{color:inherit}header,main,footer{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:24px}header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.15em;font-weight:800}h1{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(3rem,10vw,7.5rem);line-height:.9;letter-spacing:-.055em;margin:.25em 0}h2{font:700 clamp(2rem,5vw,3.7rem)/1 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.04em}.eyebrow,.tag{font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:800}.hero{padding:5vw 0 3vw}.intro{font-size:clamp(1.15rem,2.5vw,1.6rem);line-height:1.4;max-width:760px}.panel{background:#fffaf0;border:2px solid #192638;border-radius:20px;box-shadow:7px 7px 0 #192638;padding:clamp(20px,4vw,48px);margin:32px 0}.dark{background:#192638;color:#fff8e7}.badge{display:inline-block;background:#ed674d;color:#192638;border:2px solid #192638;border-radius:100px;padding:10px 16px;font-weight:800}.legend{display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.85rem}.dot{display:inline-block;width:14px;height:14px;border:2px solid currentColor;border-radius:50%;background:#ed674d}.year{display:grid;grid-template-columns:75px 1fr 40px;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #b5b1a4}.dots{display:flex;gap:5px;flex-wrap:wrap}.ball{width:24px;height:24px;border:2px solid #192638;border-radius:50%;background:#ed674d}.ball.big{background:#f5bd43}.rentrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:150px 1fr 120px;gap:10px;align-items:center;margin:26px 0}.track{height:32px;background:#e3dfd0;position:relative;border-radius:40px}.bar{height:100%;background:#61b9a4;border:2px solid #192638;border-radius:40px}.range{position:absolute;top:-5px;height:42px;border-left:3px solid #ed674d;border-right:3px solid #ed674d;background:#ed674d44}.axis{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:.75rem;margin-left:160px;margin-right:130px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.9rem}td,th{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #bcb7a9;padding:10px 6px}details{overflow-x:auto}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:800;padding:15px 0}p{line-height:1.6}footer{font-size:.85rem}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:4px solid #ed674d;outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:650px){header{gap:12px}.rentrow{grid-template-columns:1fr auto}.track{grid-column:1/-1;grid-row:2}.axis{margin:0}.year{grid-template-columns:55px 1fr 30px}.ball{width:19px;height:19px}table{min-width:600px}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{scroll-behavior:auto!important;animation:none!important}}</style>